                <pb facs="0224" n="130" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg130"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No.
                        683.—Telegram.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Dardon to
                        President Barillas</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-07-07"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 7,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The political events in Guatemala have caused alarm to this Government. It is
                    said that troops are on march for the frontier. Send me instructions, so that I
                    may know what to do.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dardon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
